    "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal commit of ADR-057. Marks the ADR as Implemented with a **test-verified delta** — 6 new tests proving every layer of the `parent_content_height` threading.\n\n## The verified delta\n\n**669 / 2562 all pass** (was 663 / 2550). **6 new tests prove every layer:**\n\n| Test | Proves |\n|---|---|\n| `html height:100%` → 600 | `<html>` special case fires (uses `viewport_h`) |\n| `html,body height:100%` chains → 600 | Full `html→body→x` propagation |\n| `height:50%` on fixed 200px parent → 100 | `%` resolves against explicit parent height |\n| `height:50%` on auto parent → skips | **CSS spec correctness** — auto parent gives 0 |\n| `max-height:30%` on fixed parent → 60 | Guard removal + `parse_length_for_height` works |\n| `min-height:50%` on fixed parent → 100 | Same |\n\n**Zero existing test changes.**\n\n## What shipped\n\n- `LengthContext::parent_content_height`\n- `parse_length_for_height()` — trailing `%` resolves against parent height\n- `layout_element` threads through 8 recursive call sites\n- 3 skip guards removed (`height`, `min-height`, `max-height`)\n- `<html>` special case: `html { height: 100% }` resolves against `viewport_h`\n- `layout()` + `layout_with_pseudo()` signatures extended (protects `render_pipeline.cpp`)\n\n## Honest corrections to the spec\n\n### 1. \"Test at line 109 flips\" was wrong\n\nThe ADR spec claimed the `\"height: percentage skipped\"` test would flip after ADR-057. **It doesn't** — its `run()` uses default `viewport_height=0`, so `%` correctly resolves to 0 and the skip is still right for that setup.\n\n**The 6 new tests fill the gap** by passing explicit `viewport_height=600` and asserting `%` resolution under real conditions.\n\n**The stale comment** (\"no parent_content_height\") — factually false since ADR-057 — is now corrected in-place. Test renamed to `\"height: percentage with default viewport_h=0 skips\"`.\n\n### 2. Definition-body split-declaration bug\n\nFirst attempt updated `.hpp` declarations but missed `.cpp` definition bodies → `'parent_content_height' was not declared` build error. Fixed before checkpoint. **Same class of split-declaration bug as ADR-051's `parse_operand` discovery.**\n\n## The circularity constraint (honest)\n\n`layout_element` recurses into children first, then applies its own explicit `height:`. **Auto-height parents don't know their own content height during child layout.**\n\n**CSS spec**: child `%` height on auto parent → auto (skip). **Correct behavior, not a limitation.** Chromium/Firefox/WebKit all do this.\n\n**Consequence**: visible delta is narrower than the deferral list suggests. `%` heights on auto-height parents still skip. Only `%` on **fixed-height** parents resolve.\n\n## Visible delta\n\n**`html, body { height: 100% }` now resolves** — the CSS reset used by nearly every site starts working. Body background extends to full viewport on short pages.\n\n## The magnifier chain (after ADR-057)\n\n| Layer | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `background-image` renders | ✅ ADR-056 |\n| `parent_content_height` available | ✅ **ADR-057 (this PR)** |\n| `top: 50%` resolves | ⏸ ADR-058 |\n| `translateY(-50%)` centers | ⏸ ADR-058 |\n\n**Why `top: 50%` isn't shipped here**: alone it moves the magnifier from `y=7` to `y=28` (bottom of container, worse). Only with `translateY(-50%)` does it land at `y=18` (centered). ADR-058 ships both together.\n\n## Deferrals closed\n\n- **ADR-039's `%` height skip** — closed\n- **ADR-053's `%` max-height skip** — closed\n- **ADR-053's `%` min-height skip** — closed\n- **ADR-053's \"parent_content_height threading\" deferral** — closed\n\nMax-width/max-height now resolve the full length grammar: px / em / rem / vw / vh / vmin / vmax / % / calc() / min() / max() / clamp().\n\n## Test count\n\n- 663 → 669 cases (+6)\n- 2550 → 2562 assertions (+12)\n- Documentation + test comment only; no code changes in this PR\n\nRefs #252\n",
